                <head>No. 565.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-22"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 22, 1888</date>
                        (Received March 23.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 19th
                    instant, suggesting that each Government should beat liberty to publish the
                    joint protocols of the Samoan conference, I have the honor to inform you that
                    Her Majesty’s Government are of opinion that, pending the re-assembling of the
                    conference, its proceedings should be considered confidential, and that the
                    publication of them at present might prejudice the satisfactory solution of the
                    question.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S.
                    Sackville-West.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
